# Testing and Debugging

## Canonical suites

See [BUILD.md](../BUILD.md#verification) for the local verification targets.
Use the repository-owned embedded fixture as shipped; do not substitute a
container or a previously running server.

- `make test` prebuilds the workspace and standalone `cosmic-text` suites,
  starts one checksum-pinned embedded runtime, exports its private URL and
  credentials in `require` mode, and unloads models and terminates the owned
  process group at exit. A developer's `LEMONADE_URL`, `UFORGE_LEMOND_PATH`,
  or provisioning skip flag must not replace this fixture. Tests share the
  app's XDG model/backend cache; optional live tests can skip when their
  required models are not cached.
- `make test-ci` disables provisioning, excludes the Lemonade test namespace
  and specific cross-module live tests, forces `UFORGE_INTEGRATION_TESTS=skip`,
  and removes external URLs and credentials from the workspace test process.

Keep `TEST_THREADS=1` (the Make default) for the live suite. Its tests compete
for GPU/NPU resources on one server. Also use `--test-threads=1` when running
live tests directly; use Cargo filters for focused iteration only. For example,
to debug storage without contacting a live server:

```bash
UFORGE_INTEGRATION_TESTS=skip UFORGE_SKIP_EMBEDDED_LEMONADE=1 \
  cargo test -p u-forge-core graph::storage -- --nocapture
```

## Storage fixtures

Give each storage test a fresh `KnowledgeGraph` in its own `TempDir`.
`KnowledgeGraph::new(temp_dir.path())` creates `knowledge.db` in that directory.
Bind the directory to a named variable (e.g. `_tmp`, not `_`) that outlives
the graph, since the directory is deleted when the guard drops.

