## Lemonade integration tests — skip guard

Use `require_integration_url!()` from
[u-forge-core's test helpers](../crates/u-forge-core/src/test_helpers.rs).
For direct `cargo test`, `UFORGE_INTEGRATION_TESTS` controls the guard:

- Unset or empty: [resolve an external URL](environment-config.mdc#lemonade-connection-selection),
  or skip with a diagnostic if none is found.
- `require`: the same resolution, but fail if it yields no URL. The
  canonical suite sets this mode with its own `LEMONADE_URL`; hosted CI
  does not use it.
- `skip`: skip even when a server is available.
- Explicit API base URL: health-check that URL or fail.

Live GPU/CPU LLM tests are pinned to `Gemma-4-E4B-it-GGUF` and skip when it is
not downloaded; they must not fall back to the production model preference
order because that can load a much larger model during the serial test flow.
Use `gemma4-it-e4b-FLM` for any live NPU LLM test. Embedding and STT integration
tests already use comparatively small capability-specific models.

